module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.AssociatedSiteRefinement
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.LisseEtaleSite
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.SubcategoryRingedTopos
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Stacks.SubcategorySite
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Cocontinuous.LowerShriekFullyFaithful
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Topos.MorphismOfTopoi

/-!
# The inclusion of the lisse-étale site, reduced to one closure property

Stacks 0788 (1) asserts that the inclusion of the lisse-étale site of an algebraic stack `𝒳`
into its étale site is fully faithful, continuous and cocontinuous, and derives from that the
morphism of topoi `g : Sh(𝒳_{lisse,étale}) → Sh(𝒳_{étale})` whose inverse image is restriction,
together with the lower-shriek functor left adjoint to it on abelian sheaves.

This file is the lisse-étale sibling of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Stacks/FlatFppfInclusion.lean`, and has the same shape. Full
faithfulness is `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.fullyFaithfulι`. Continuity and cocontinuity are
the étale case of **Stacks 07AK**, proved as
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isContinuous_ι_etaleTopology` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.isCocontinuous_ι_etaleTopology`, whose one hypothesis is the closure
condition of 07AK (1): *an object of `𝒳` admitting a morphism to a smooth object, lying over a
smooth morphism of schemes, is itself smooth.*

**Nothing here carries a `@[stacks]` tag.** Each statement takes the closure property as an
explicit hypothesis, so none of them is the statement of 0788, and the tag is left for whoever
discharges the hypothesis. This is the bridge pattern of the flat-fppf sibling, and of the
relative properties of §04XB before it.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.ClosedUnderSmoothMorphisms`: the closure condition of
  **Stacks 07AK** (1) for the smooth objects of an algebraic stack, which is the hypothesis of
  everything below.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.inclusionTopology`: the topology of the lisse-étale site
  in the sense of the source.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.toposMorphism` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.toposMorphismTopology`: the morphism of topoi `g` of
  **Stacks 0788** (1)(a), conditional on that property, at each of the two descriptions of the
  topology.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.abelianLowerShriek` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.abelianLowerShriekAdjunction`: the functor `g_!` on
  abelian sheaves and its adjunction `g_! ⊣ g⁻¹`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.etaleRingedTopos`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.ringedTopos` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.ringedToposMorphism`: the two ringed topoi of
  **Stacks 0788** (1) and the morphism of ringed topoi between them, the étale instance of
  `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Stacks/SubcategoryRingedTopos.lean`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.map_mem_etalePrecoverage`: the image in the category of
  all schemes of a chosen étale covering family of the big site is an étale covering family.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.isContinuous_inclusion` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.isCocontinuous_inclusion`: continuity and cocontinuity of
  the inclusion, conditional on the closure property.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.topology_le_inclusionTopology`: the topology generated by
  the chosen étale covering families between smooth objects is coarser than the topology the
  site inherits from `𝒳_{étale}`. This holds with no hypothesis.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.inclusionTopology_le_topology` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.inclusionTopology_eq_topology`: the converse inequality,
  conditional on the closure property, and hence the equality of the two descriptions of the
  topology of the lisse-étale site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.isContinuous_inclusion_topology` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.isCocontinuous_inclusion_topology`: continuity and
  cocontinuity of the inclusion for that generated topology.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.isIso_abelianLowerShriek_unit` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.isIso_abelianPushforward_counit`: the unit of `g_! ⊣ g⁻¹`
  and the counit of `g⁻¹ ⊣ g_*` are isomorphisms, which is **Stacks 077I** for this inclusion.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.isFlat_ringedToposMorphism`: the morphism of ringed topoi
  is flat (**Stacks 04JB**).

## Implementation notes

The topology used here is `P.ι.inheritedTopology (associatedTopology … (etaleTopology B))` for
`P = AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.smoothObject`, i.e. the topology in which a family of morphisms of
smooth objects covers exactly when its image covers in `𝒳_{étale}`. That is the definition the
source gives — "a family of morphisms of `𝒳_{lisse,étale}` which forms a covering of
`𝒳_{étale}`" — and it is the topology the 07AK results are stated for, so no new
Grothendieck topology is introduced. The sibling `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.LisseEtale.topology`
of `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Stacks/LisseEtaleSite.lean` is the topology generated by the
*chosen* covering families of the ambient site; `topology_le_inclusionTopology` compares the
two, in the direction that holds with no hypothesis at all: a chosen étale family of smooth
objects is a family of strongly cartesian morphisms whose image covers, because the inclusion of
a full subcategory is fully faithful and every morphism of a category fibred in groupoids is
strongly cartesian over its own image.

The converse inequality, `inclusionTopology_le_topology`, is the assertion with content — every
étale covering sieve of a smooth object has to be refined by a chosen étale covering family with
smooth sources — and it needs the closure property. It is the étale instance of the refinement
lemma `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.exists_etaleCovering_le_of_mem_associatedTopology` together with
that property: the members of a chosen étale family are étale, hence smooth, so the sources the
refinement produces are smooth objects. The two topologies are therefore equal
(`inclusionTopology_eq_topology`), again conditionally, and no third topology is introduced.
Continuity transfers from a topology to a smaller one and cocontinuity transfers the other way,
so both assertions are recorded at both descriptions, the equality being what carries
cocontinuity across.

The morphism of topoi is the cocontinuous one: `g_*` is
`CategoryTheory.Functor.sheafPushforwardCocontinuous` and `g⁻¹` is
`CategoryTheory.Functor.sheafPushforwardContinuous`, i.e. restriction along the inclusion on the
nose, which is the form 0788 (1)(a) requires; left exactness of restriction is then automatic.

The abelian layer is the general theory of **Stacks 077I**
(`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Cocontinuous/LowerShriekFullyFaithful.lean`) specialised to
this inclusion: no construction is repeated, because the inclusion satisfies that file's three
hypotheses — continuous, cocontinuous and fully faithful — as soon as the closure property
holds. The coefficient category is forced to be `Ab.{u + 1}`: the two sites live in
`Type (u + 1)` with morphisms in `Type u`, and that file takes abelian groups at the maximum of
those two universes.

The ringed layer is the étale instance of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Stacks/SubcategoryRingedTopos.lean`, which does the work for an
arbitrary full subsite of the site of a category fibred in groupoids, so the lisse-étale and
flat-fppf cases are two instantiations rather than two constructions. It needs essential
smallness of the fppf site of `𝒳` as an instance hypothesis, because the structure sheaf of
**Stacks 06TV** takes its sections in `Type u` while the site lives in `Type (u + 1)`; that
hypothesis is `AlgebraicGeometry.Stack.essentiallySmall_obj`'s conclusion.

